      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Understanding brain organization of speech production has been a principal goal of neuroscience. Historically, brain speech production has been associated with so-called Broca\u2019s area (Brodmann area \u2013BA- 44 and 45), however, modern neuroimaging developments suggest speech production is associated with networks rather than with areas. The purpose of this paper was to analyze the connectivity of BA47 ( pars orbitalis) in relation to language ."
        },
        {
          "Label": "METHOD",
          "content": "A meta-analysis was conducted to assess the language network in which BA47 is involved. The Brainmap database was used. Twenty papers corresponding to 29 experimental conditions with a total of 373 subjects were included."
        },
        {
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Our results suggest that BA47 participates in a \u201cfrontal language production system\u201d (or extended Broca\u2019s system). The BA47  connectivity found is also concordant with a minor role in language semantics."
        },
        {
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "BA47 plays a central role in the language production system."
        }
      ]},
